(7254545, 1126620, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b> <br/>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:<br/>We try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us. If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so. then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping! </b> <br/> <br/>You nailed the Challenge with your vanishing point railroad track - and I"m glad you didn''t get squashed by a train in doing so.  <br/> <br/>If this was my image, I''d probably go for more dark tones to go with the predominantly light tones you selected in processing.  This would give the image more drama and make it stand out among the competition.  As you know, there were quite a few train track shots in this Challenge.  <br/> <br/>More dark tones to balance the lighter ones and perhaps more emphasis on the cloudy sky, I think would have pulled this image from the nice mid-five score you received to a higher number.</td>', ' GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:We try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us. If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so. then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping!   You nailed the Challenge with your vanishing point railroad track - and I"m glad you didn''t get squashed by a train in doing so.   If this was my image, I''d probably go for more dark tones to go with the predominantly light tones you selected in processing.  This would give the image more drama and make it stand out among the competition.  As you know, there were quite a few train track shots in this Challenge.   More dark tones to balance the lighter ones and perhaps more emphasis on the cloudy sky, I think would have pulled this image from the nice mid-five score you received to a higher number.', '2014-08-24 12:13:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254546, 1127152, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue - colors are brilliant, realistic, and well saturated, while staying within believable ranges.<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast - a nice bright image, and good control of the lighting, so that the highlights are not blown out.<br/> <br/>Foes is and depth of field - good depth of field, focus is sharp overall.  <br/> <br/>Subjective - the image looks a bit over processed to me.  The clouds in the sky are just starting to pixilate in the thin areas of the clouds.  The vegetation also seems to have suffered a bit.  The boardwalk makes a great set of leading lines, but to what?  There does not seem to be a true vanishing point.  The end of the walk sys to me, more cut off than vanished.  <br/> <br/>Summary - overall I like the image, throw in a sailboat in the right spot, and you have a killer leading lines image.  A little further back so the hand rails almost meet, and I think it would have scored better, as well.</td>', 'Critique Club Review Color Saturation and Hue - colors are brilliant, realistic, and well saturated, while staying within believable ranges. Brightness and Contrast - a nice bright image, and good control of the lighting, so that the highlights are not blown out. Foes is and depth of field - good depth of field, focus is sharp overall.   Subjective - the image looks a bit over processed to me.  The clouds in the sky are just starting to pixilate in the thin areas of the clouds.  The vegetation also seems to have suffered a bit.  The boardwalk makes a great set of leading lines, but to what?  There does not seem to be a true vanishing point.  The end of the walk sys to me, more cut off than vanished.   Summary - overall I like the image, throw in a sailboat in the right spot, and you have a killer leading lines image.  A little further back so the hand rails almost meet, and I think it would have scored better, as well.', '2014-08-24 12:13:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254548, 1127155, 14476, '<td valign="top"><br/> <br/><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:<br/>We try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us. If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so. then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping! </b> <br/> <br/>Well, Janine, you ticked the box and received the best score you can get in a Challenge.  Therefore it''s difficult to find anything to critique in this fine image that our fellow DPCers have found to be the best of the bunch.<br/> <br/>So, I would suggest that, if you have the time and energy, join the Critique Club and help others with their photography!  It''s fun and a new challenge, for sure.</td>', ' GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:We try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us. If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so. then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping!   Well, Janine, you ticked the box and received the best score you can get in a Challenge.  Therefore it''s difficult to find anything to critique in this fine image that our fellow DPCers have found to be the best of the bunch. So, I would suggest that, if you have the time and energy, join the Critique Club and help others with their photography!  It''s fun and a new challenge, for sure.', '2014-08-24 12:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254560, 1126909, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue - colors are done with an overall blue hue.  Looking at the details outside of the walkway, it appears the the lighting gives this effect, as opposed to manipulation by the photographer.<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast - lighting is well done.  A bit of burnout on some of the overhead lights, which distracts a tiny bit.  <br/> <br/>Focus and Depth of Field - Nice sharp focus, and a deep depth of field.  Both work well in this image.<br/> <br/>Subjective - as mentioned the Wells Fargo, and eBank signs distract.  Since this is advanced editing, the distractions on the outside could have been darkened to the point they no longer commanded attention.  The camera angle seem a bit tilted, or an least not square to the subject, so that the image seems to be off level.  <br/> <br/>Summary - I like the image a lot.  Cloning out the bright dot, at the end of the bridge would have left the four blue lights more pronounced.  They would look even more mysterious and ominous than they do now.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color Saturation and Hue - colors are done with an overall blue hue.  Looking at the details outside of the walkway, it appears the the lighting gives this effect, as opposed to manipulation by the photographer. Brightness and Contrast - lighting is well done.  A bit of burnout on some of the overhead lights, which distracts a tiny bit.   Focus and Depth of Field - Nice sharp focus, and a deep depth of field.  Both work well in this image. Subjective - as mentioned the Wells Fargo, and eBank signs distract.  Since this is advanced editing, the distractions on the outside could have been darkened to the point they no longer commanded attention.  The camera angle seem a bit tilted, or an least not square to the subject, so that the image seems to be off level.   Summary - I like the image a lot.  Cloning out the bright dot, at the end of the bridge would have left the four blue lights more pronounced.  They would look even more mysterious and ominous than they do now.', '2014-08-24 12:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254913, 1126909, 74588, '<td valign="top">like the of-world colour:)</td>', 'like the of-world colour:)', '2014-08-25 08:20:47.000000', NULL, 0),
